SCOPE — please read this first

This repository contains code from several sources, and only this
project's own work is covered by the MIT license below.

  COVERED by the MIT license (original work in this project):
      every file in this repository EXCEPT the ones listed under NOT
      COVERED - the Python modules at the top level and in common/,
      dashboard/, evaluation/, exploration/, reporting/, rewards/,
      training/, tools/ and tests/; dashboard/web/ (except
      dashboard/web/static/vendor/); docs/ and the other documentation and
      configuration files; and the trained model weights:
      glitch_hunter_main_brain.zip, glitch_hunter_main_brain_coverage.npz
                                          (the final 16M brain, in this
                                           repository and as a GitHub
                                           Release asset)
      mario_brain_checkpoint.zip          (the 6M brain, in this
                                           repository's history)

  NOT COVERED — third-party, different terms, see docs/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md:
      games/mario_clean/          (the Super Mario Bros clone and its assets)
      games/mario_bugged/         (a copy of it, for deliberate QA test bugs)
      dashboard/web/static/vendor/
                                  (the Socket.IO client - its own MIT license;
                                   the Press Start 2P font - SIL Open Font
                                   License 1.1)
      the game's graphics wherever they appear, including the screenshots
      and recordings in docs/assets/ and in every incident report

The games/mario_clean/ and games/mario_bugged/ directories are someone else's work
(two copies of one game) and its upstream project
carries no open-source license at all. Do not assume the MIT terms below
apply to it. docs/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md explains what is and isn't permitted.
